  "name": "Nord Drum 3P",
  "manufacturer": "Nord",
  "family": "Drum",
  "status": "experimental",
  "trust": "local",
  "description": "Nord Drum 3P drum synthesizer: every control of its manual's MIDI CC list.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "type": "manual",
      "title": "Nord Drum 3P User Manual, OS v1.x, Edition C",
      "notes": "MIDI controller list (page 15 of the PDF) read by tools/profiles/nord/read-nord-cc.mjs from Nord Drum 3P English User Manual v1.x Edition C.pdf (sha256 b861ece3e397658c85a5437d6ffb4a7aa52fda383d0911ab8aac9fbc4aadf138), https://www.nordkeyboards.com/wt/documents/97/Nord%20Drum%203P%20English%20User%20Manual%20v1.x%20Edition%20C.pdf. Not yet checked against the instrument itself."
    }
  ],
  "testedWith": [],
  "authoringNotes": [
    "Generated by tools/profiles/nord/make-profiles.mjs; edit the layout in tools/profiles/nord/synths/, not this file.",
    "Every parameter is a row of the manual's MIDI controller list, with its printed name, sent as the control change it prints on the channel variable. Nothing here has been sent to a real instrument yet.",
    "The list prints controller numbers only: every value is 0 - 127, and a setting chosen from a list (a model, a waveform, an effect type) is a number here, not a choice.",
    "The manual: a control has the same controller on every drum channel, sent on the Global MIDI channel to the channel selected (Channel Select, CC 70). Set the channel variable to the Global MIDI channel.",
    "Tone Pitch is two controllers, MSB and LSB, laid out as printed.",
    "Left out, the pedals, the wheel and bank select: 0 Bank Select MSB, 32 Bank Select LSB."
  ],
